# The libraries sdkgen knows how to generate, and how to read each one.
#
#     library <name> <install-name> <tbd path inside the SDK>
#     language c | objective-c
#     pass <umbrella header in tools/sdkgen/headers> [-D<macro>=<value>]...
#
# <name> is what tools/sdkgen.sh is given on its command line.  The database is
# written for <install-name>, into the file named after its last component.
# The .tbd is read for every document in it, and a library it re-exports is
# folded into the export list when a program linked against this one imports
# that library's symbols by this one's ordinal: when it names a parent
# umbrella, which is what marks the libraries under /usr/lib/system as parts of
# libSystem rather than libraries of their own, or when its install name is
# outside the public locations the linker links directly, which is what makes
# UIFoundation and CollectionViewCore in /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks
# parts of AppKit.  CoreFoundation re-exports libobjc, Foundation re-exports
# CoreFoundation and libobjc, and AppKit re-exports Foundation and
# ApplicationServices, all public, so each keeps its exports in its own file:
# an x86_64 program linked against AppKit alone gets a load command of its own
# for CoreGraphics, which ApplicationServices re-exports, and imports
# CGContextFillRect from there.
#
# A library's headers are parsed as C unless it names objective-c, which
# libobjc, Foundation and AppKit do because their headers declare classes and
# protocols that plain C cannot parse.  The .layouts file records the language
# so tools/sdkgen/layout_check.sh compiles its probe the same way.
#
# Each pass is parsed twice, for x86_64 and for arm64, and an export takes its
# declaration from the first pass whose x86_64 parse spells it.  libSystem needs
# four, because two families of variant entry points are declared only under a
# macro that would rename the plain entry point if it were set in the first
# pass: the $NOCANCEL variants of the cancellation points want
# __DARWIN_NON_CANCELABLE, and the $DARWIN_EXTSN variants of fopen, fdopen,
# popen, getgroups, select and pselect want _DARWIN_C_SOURCE, and pselect and
# select have a variant with both suffixes.
#
# libncurses is here for the shell rather than for curses programs: /bin/sh
# execs bash, which links it for readline's terminal handling, and system and
# popen start their command under /bin/sh.
library libSystem /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib usr/lib/libSystem.B.tbd
pass libSystem.h
pass libSystem.h -D__DARWIN_NON_CANCELABLE=1
pass libSystem.h -D_DARWIN_C_SOURCE
pass libSystem.h -D_DARWIN_C_SOURCE -D__DARWIN_NON_CANCELABLE=1

